# Warren update-channel Ed25519 metadata signing public keys.
#
# Each non-comment, non-empty line is a single 64-character hex-encoded
# Ed25519 verifying key. Comments start with `#`. Trailing whitespace is
# stripped per `parse_keys` in `src/defaults.rs`.
#
# This key can ship an installer to every user, so it is the highest-
# privilege key in the system. It is dedicated to app updates and was
# generated/kept OFFLINE. Do NOT reuse the relay/admin signing key
# (online, and its lineage was burned once:
# `admin/admin-signing.key.BURNED-committed-do-not-use`).
#
# The matching Ed25519 secret is stored OFFLINE by poka and as the CI
# secret `WARREN_UPDATE_SIGNING_KEY` (used by `release.yml` to sign every
# published `*.json` manifest). A `warren-vpn` daemon shipped with this
# trust file accepts manifests signed by the key below and rejects all
# others (fail-closed).
#
# Key rotation: add the new pubkey on its own line (both are then trusted
# during the overlap), ship a release, then drop the retired line.
